From 9c95a742b585d59360e391edcef88e52fb619f9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vandomas <vandcim@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:56:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] zink: put the buffer view cache key first

equals_bufferview_key() compares a zink_bufferview_key against the start
of the stored zink_buffer_view, but that object starts with pres, so a
lookup never matches and every get_buffer_view() call creates another
VkBufferView that lives as long as the resource. Move the key to the
front, the layout zink_surface already uses, so lookups compare the
right bytes and existing views get reused.

With a texture buffer rebound between two ranges 50k times, resident
memory grew by 103 MB before and 7 MB after on Mesa 26.2.2 with
MoltenVK, and by 129 MB before and 40 MB after on main with KosmicKrisp,
with identical GPU results. In a Beyond All Reason replay the driver
created 44094 buffer views before and 12 after, reusing cached views
40834 times. The mismatch and the fix were found by Anatolii, who also
did the measurements.

Fixes: 5cfaa6cd5fcb ("zink: use smaller keys for surface/bufferview caching and switch to sets")
Cc: mesa-stable
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44358>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_types.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_types.h b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_types.h
index 34bcaf61d29..a3739643a17 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_types.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_types.h
@@ -1611,8 +1611,8 @@ struct zink_bufferview_key {
 };
 
 struct zink_buffer_view {
-   struct pipe_resource *pres;
    struct zink_bufferview_key key;
+   struct pipe_resource *pres;
    VkBufferView buffer_view;
 };
 
